  DEMO_BASE    Industrials    49.60   50.80   49.60   50.80    1.00x
  DEMO_FALL    Utilities      47.62   46.75   45.88   45.00    1.00x
  DEMO_QUIET   Industrials    50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    1.00x
  DEMO_GOOD    Technology     50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x
  DEMO_WIDE    Technology     50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x
  DEMO_NOSTOP  Technology     50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x
  DEMO_WEAK    Utilities      50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x
  DEMO_TIE_A   Industrials    50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x
  DEMO_TIE_B   Industrials    50.80   49.60   50.80   54.50    3.00x

==== STAGE 2 of 9: STAGE CLASSIFICATION ====
  Does: places each stock in Stage 1-4 by its close against the 30-week moving
        average (MA).
        Stage 2: the MA rising (up over 0.5% in 4 weeks) and the close above it in
        most of the last 6 weeks.
        Stage 4: the MA falling and the close mostly below it.
        With a flat MA the stage is decided by last week's: Stage 1 after a base or
        a decline, Stage 3 after an advance.
  In:   the weekly closes, and last Friday's stage (state the strategy carries).
  Out:  this Friday's stage. A change of stage number is a transition.

  ticker             MA  4w slope  wks>MA  last Friday      this Friday
  DEMO_BASE       50.07    +0.10%     3/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 1 (wk 30)
  DEMO_FALL       53.46    -6.14%     0/6  Stage 4 (wk 30)  Stage 4 (wk 31)
  DEMO_QUIET      50.53    +0.62%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_GOOD       50.53    +0.62%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_WIDE       49.66    +1.04%     6/6  Stage 1 (wk 13)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_NOSTOP     50.36    +0.73%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_WEAK       50.53    +0.62%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_TIE_A      50.53    +0.62%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2
  DEMO_TIE_B      50.53    +0.62%     4/6  Stage 1 (wk 29)  Stage 2 (wk 1)  <- Stage 1 to 2

==== STAGE 3 of 9: MACRO GATE ====
  Does: reads the market as a whole from weighted indicators. The confidence is the
        Bullish share of the weight of the indicators that are not Neutral.
        A Bearish market blocks new buys and a Bullish one blocks new shorts; a
        Neutral one allows new buys and blocks new shorts.
  In:   the index DEMO_INDEX; the A-D line and global indices too when supplied (none here).
  Out:  the market trend, and which side may open new positions.

  index: Stage 2 (wk 1), MA 1225.59 Rising (+0.83%)
  indicator Index Stage    Bullish  weight 3.0  Index in Stage 2 (advancing)
  indicator A-D Line       Neutral  weight 2.0  No A-D data
  indicator Momentum Index Neutral  weight 2.0  No A-D data
  indicator NH-NL          Bullish  weight 1.5  Index trending higher over 3 months (NH-NL proxy positive)
  indicator Global Markets Neutral  weight 1.5  No global data
  confidence 1.00 -> trend Bullish (Bullish above 0.65, Bearish below 0.35)
  => new longs open, new shorts closed.

==== STAGE 4 of 9: SECTORS AND PRE-SCREEN ====
  Does: rates each sector from its ETF's stage and relative strength (RS) against
        the index. A Stage 2 stock in a Weak sector is not bought, a Stage 4 stock
        in a Strong sector is not shorted, and only Stage 2 and 4 stocks go on.
  In:   each sector ETF's weekly bars, the index, and each stock's stage.
  Out:  a rating per sector, and the stocks that go on to full analysis.

  sector       ETF          ETF stage        rating
  Technology   DEMO_XTECH   Stage 2 (wk 31)  Strong
  Industrials  DEMO_XIND    Stage 1 (wk 30)  Neutral
  Utilities    DEMO_XUTIL   Stage 4 (wk 31)  Weak

  DEMO_BASE    Stage 1 (wk 30)  stops: neither Stage 2 (buy) nor Stage 4 (short)
  DEMO_FALL    Stage 4 (wk 31)  goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_QUIET   Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_GOOD    Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_WIDE    Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_NOSTOP  Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_WEAK    Stage 2 (wk 1)   stops: its sector (Utilities) blocks this side
  DEMO_TIE_A   Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis
  DEMO_TIE_B   Stage 2 (wk 1)   goes on to full analysis

==== STAGE 5 of 9: BREAKOUT CASCADE ====
  Does: checks each analysed stock against the buy rules in order; the first rule it
        fails is where it stops. Long rules:
        price floor (off)
        -> stage setup: a Stage 1 to 2 transition, or Stage 2 for at most 4 weeks;
        or Stage 2 at any age when the breakout reaches new high ground (above every
        weekly high of the last 10 years, or with no overhead supply in the last 130
        weeks)
        -> breakout volume: at least 1.5x the prior 4 weeks
        -> RS not declining
        -> failed breakout (off)
        -> volume band (off)
  In:   per analysed stock: stage, breakout-week volume, RS against the index.
  Out:  where each stock stopped, per side.

  ticker       side   stage            volume           RS                 result
  DEMO_FALL    long   Stage 4 (wk 31)  Weak 1.00x       Negative_declining stopped at the breakout gate: stage setup
  DEMO_QUIET   long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Weak 1.00x       Bullish_crossover  stopped at the breakout gate: breakout volume
  DEMO_GOOD    long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Strong 3.00x     Bullish_crossover  passed the breakout gates: scored below
  DEMO_WIDE    long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Strong 3.00x     Bullish_crossover  passed the breakout gates: scored below
  DEMO_NOSTOP  long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Strong 3.00x     Bullish_crossover  passed the breakout gates: scored below
  DEMO_TIE_A   long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Strong 3.00x     Bullish_crossover  passed the breakout gates: scored below
  DEMO_TIE_B   long   Stage 2 (wk 1)   Strong 3.00x     Bullish_crossover  passed the breakout gates: scored below
  No stock was checked as a short: the macro gate (stage 3) closed new shorts.

==== STAGE 6 of 9: SCORING ====
  Does: adds up points for each signal a breakout carries, and grades the total:
        A+ >= 85, A >= 70, B >= 55, C >= 40, D >= 25. The lowest grade bought is C.
  In:   the stocks that passed the breakout gates.
  Out:  a score and a grade per stock; a grade below the lowest stops it.

  DEMO_GOOD    score 105, grade A+
                +30  Stage1→Stage2 breakout
                +20  Strong volume
                +30  RS bullish crossover
                +15  Virgin territory
                +10  Strong sector
  DEMO_WIDE    score 105, grade A+
                +30  Stage1→Stage2 breakout
                +20  Strong volume
                +30  RS bullish crossover
                +15  Virgin territory
                +10  Strong sector
  DEMO_NOSTOP  score 105, grade A+
                +30  Stage1→Stage2 breakout
                +20  Strong volume
                +30  RS bullish crossover
                +15  Clean overhead
                +10  Strong sector
  DEMO_TIE_A   score 95, grade A+
                +30  Stage1→Stage2 breakout
                +20  Strong volume
                +30  RS bullish crossover
                +15  Virgin territory
  DEMO_TIE_B   score 95, grade A+
                +30  Stage1→Stage2 breakout
                +20  Strong volume
                +30  RS bullish crossover
                +15  Virgin territory

==== STAGE 7 of 9: RANKING ====
  Does: orders the graded stocks by score, highest first. Equal scores go by a hash
        of the ticker and the date (2024-06-28) seeded with 7 (demo setting; the
        default is 0), smallest first.
        Only the top names on each side go on to the entry walk:
        longs: max_buy_candidates = 4 (demo setting; the default is 20)
        shorts: max_short_candidates = 10
  In:   the graded stocks.
  Out:  the ranked list, and the cut.

    #  ticker       side  score  grade  tiebreak key
    1  DEMO_WIDE    long    105  A+     819791371
    2  DEMO_NOSTOP  long    105  A+     3038072267
    3  DEMO_GOOD    long    105  A+     3174679561
    4  DEMO_TIE_B   long     95  A+     2195971111
  ----- cut: only the top 4 long names go on -----
    5  DEMO_TIE_A   long     95  A+     2212748730

==== STAGE 8 of 9: ENTRY WALK ====
  Does: takes the names above the cut in rank order. The trigger is the last close.
        Initial stop: 4.0% (half of 8.0%) under the lowest low since the highest
        high of the last 90 trading days, when that low is 8.0% or more below that
        high. With no such low it is a fallback stop, 4.0% under the trigger. A stop
        at or up to $0.125 above a half-dollar is moved to $0.125 below it.
        Skipped: a stop more than 15.0% below the trigger (book 5.1), and a fallback
        stop, since require_structural_stop is on (demo setting; the default is
        off), as in the investor preset.
        Shares: as many as put 1.0% of the portfolio at risk between trigger and
        stop, but at most 30.0% of the portfolio in one long name (20.0% in one
        short); a name that costs more than the cash left is skipped.
  In:   the names above the cut, and $100,000.00 cash.
  Out:  an entry ticket, or the reason for skipping, per name.

  DEMO_WIDE    trigger 54.50, stop 39.92 (under the correction low), 26.8% below
               SKIPPED: stop more than 15.0% below the trigger. Cash unchanged.
  DEMO_NOSTOP  trigger 54.50, stop 52.32 (fallback: no qualifying correction low), 4.0% below
               SKIPPED: no correction low to put the stop under. Cash unchanged.
  DEMO_GOOD    trigger 54.50, stop 47.14 (under the correction low), 13.5% below
               PLACED 135 shares: risk $993.62 of the $1,000.00 budget, cost $7,357.50
               cash $100,000.00 -> $92,642.50
  DEMO_TIE_B   trigger 54.50, stop 47.14 (under the correction low), 13.5% below
               PLACED 135 shares: risk $993.62 of the $1,000.00 budget, cost $7,357.50
               cash $92,642.50 -> $85,285.00

==== STAGE 9 of 9: ORDERS ====
  Does: puts out the day's orders: one stop-limit entry ticket per placed name, for
        its shares. It triggers at the trigger price and does not fill more than
        2.0% past it.
        Once filled, the position starts under its initial stop.
  In:   the placed names.
  Out:  the tickets, worked from the next session.

  symbol       side   shares   trigger  initial stop
  DEMO_GOOD    long      135     54.50         47.14
  DEMO_TIE_B   long      135     54.50         47.14
